     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "MOA:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " bactericidal beta-lactams; inhibit cell wall enzymes, disrupting cell wall synth."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Treats:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " excellent vs gram (+) cocci and certain gram (-) bacilli."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Treats (gaps):"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ⍉cephalosporin covers enterococci; none covers MRSA except ceftaroline/ceftobiprole; none covers anaerobic gram (-) bacilli except cefotetan/cefoxitin."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Know:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " PO first-gen = common for uncomp SSTI (staph, strep); IV cefazolin for MSSA endocarditis and surg ppx; cephalexin = often used for uncomp UTI (E. coli, per local suscep)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Know:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " most are renally excreted (dose-adjust in renal insuff); ceftriaxone (biliary) doesn't need adj."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "CI:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " hx of major hypersensitivity to other cephalosporins."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Allergy:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " cross-reactivity w PCN = less common than thought (~2% of PCN-allergic pts); third/fourth gen or a dissimilar R1 side chain: negligible risk; cefazolin: very ↓. Give cautiously after a sig beta-lactam rxn."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Preg:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " widely considered safe; breastfeed often discouraged (may alt infant bowel flora)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
